# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion programme's four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# FXL2 (TIMED, the combination all, WP0): the LEVERS again (B2); eight live (concurrent8_steady) in the repeat pair of the ABAB, every boot a fresh reset. READ:
# c2_smoke_check clean (a lever arm also has every engaged line and no fell-back line), no stall; then PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians: python3
# scripts/ci/w2ln_timing_compare.py pair <A container log> <B container log> --window steady --a-smoke <A smoke log> --b-smoke <B smoke log> for (FXC1, FXL1) and (FXC2,
# FXL2), and its floor subcommand over the two control logs; the texts equal (text_mismatches empty). Levers on together: S1 shard argmax (QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX), K/V
# page writer (QWEN_FAST_KV_PAGE_WRITER), MLP streaming config and L1 multiply (QWEN_FAST_MLP_CFG), CCL options (QWEN_FAST_CCL_OPTIONS), WP6 F-F1 drafter local reduce
# (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_REDUCE), WP6 F-F3a drafter SwiGLU and residual kernels (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_TAIL), WP6 F-F3c drafter fused gate|up matmul (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_GATEUP1), WP6 R2
# drafter matmuls on device-width grids (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_MM_GRID), F-F2 drafter permutation kernels (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_PERMUTE), F-F3c fused drafter q|k|v projection
# (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_QKV1), F-F4 one 64-row drafter head (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_HEAD64). every lever that is exact by construction on together, to be timed and audited once before
# any ablation: the drafter permutations, S1 with the tree fold, the drafter reduce, fused q|k|v, tail kernels, fused gate|up weight and device-width matmul grids, the
# 64-row drafter head, the CCL options at the sweep winner rs-c1 (chunks per sync 1 on the unit-major reduce-scatters; exact, 5 of 5 pairs, 16.9 to 14.7 us per call), the
# K/V page writer (its card-M proof passed and is recorded in ordered_writer_evidence_tp4.json: the full run 1976 of 1976 exact, both negative controls fail), the MLP
# streaming config g3u4d3 (card-M sweep: the composed gate, up and down chain 170.4 to 162.1 us per layer, exact), the two engine-start upload levers, and the four
# host-side round-host levers (tp4/round-host: the draft selection with its codebook checks made once, the quad readback merge as one batch, the verify-time diff write
# keyed on the start and page table, the unparsed per-phase lines dropped; each declines to the reference whole on any failed check and is exact by its own audit); NOT the
# fused MLP gate|up (its kernels have never compiled on a card). Duration (estimate): 35 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady
